course: dictionary
lesson: 15377
title: Spatula: a tool for the kitchen and the lab
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name a thing you can hold. A spatula is one of them. The word tells you it is a noun, so it is a thing, not an action. Look at the words around it to picture the tool: «Flip the pancake with a spatula.» You flip with it, so it must be something that lifts and turns food.
explain: «Scrape the last of the cake mix out of the bowl with a spatula.» Scrape means move something off a surface, so the spatula must have a flat edge that can slide along the bowl. Try a test: put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. A flat tool for scraping fits, so you have the right idea.
explain: The same word can name a tool in different places. In a kitchen, a spatula spreads, mixes, scrapes or lifts food. In a science lab, «Use the spatula to scoop a little salt onto the scales» shows a small flat tool for scooping powder. The sentence tells you which job it means.
fact: A spatula is a noun: a thing, not an action.
fact: A kitchen spatula has a wide, flat, bendy blade.
fact: Spatulas are used for spreading, mixing, scraping and lifting food.
fact: In a science lab, a small flat spatula is used to scoop powders such as salt.
fact: Doctors also use a small spatula to press down your tongue.
exercise: «Flip the pancake with a spatula.» What is a spatula? | A type of cake | A hot pan you cook in | *A kitchen tool for lifting and turning food | A bowl for mixing
exercise: «Use a spatula, not your fingers, to lift the hot burger.» Why use a spatula here? | To wash the plate | *To lift the hot food safely | To make the burger colder | To play a game with the burger
exercise: Which of these is a job a spatula does? | Timing how long the food cooks | Holding water in a jug | *Scraping cake mix from a bowl | Keeping milk cold in a fridge
test: «In the lab, the teacher gave us a spatula to scoop a little salt.» What is the spatula used for here? | Cutting a sandwich in half | Stirring a hot soup in a big pan | *Scooping a small amount of powder | Carrying water to the sink
test: Which word names a thing, not an action? | scrape | flip | *spatula | spread
exam: Which sentence uses the word spatula correctly? | He spatula'd the window very loudly. | The spatula rode its bike to school. | *She flipped the pancake with a spatula. | She drank a spatula of cold milk.
